## Subagent routing

**Applies when:** Primary orchestrator chat is about to create, refactor, or implement code (not question-only or doc-only work).

- Hub-and-spoke: delegate domain work to [`.cursor/agents/`](../agents/) specialists; do not implement cross-domain edits in the orchestrator thread.
- Before substantial implementation, follow [`subagent-governance.mdc`](./subagent-governance.mdc) (scope check, provisioning, handoff).
- Registry: [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md).

Does not apply when the user is in question/review-only mode, when `feature-designer` scope is doc-only, or when a domain subagent is already executing.

**Feature hub (not a Cursor rule):** [CREATURE_GOAL_DRIVERS.md](../../Project_Docs/Draft_Features/CREATURE_GOAL_DRIVERS.md) — movement in [CREATURE_MOVEMENT_V3.md](../../Project_Docs/Draft_Features/CREATURE_MOVEMENT_V3.md), memory in [CREATURE_MEMORY.md](../../Project_Docs/Draft_Features/CREATURE_MEMORY.md).

**Archived docs:** `Completed_Features/` drift is expected unless explicitly cited.

# Session Metadata Rule **Cursor only, not to be used by Claude**
At the very end of every response, output a single, ultra-brief markdown line showing estimated token usage and remaining capacity. Use the format:
`[Context: ~X / Max Y tokens (Z% used)]`
Do not write conversational filler surrounding this metric.
